    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95">

                <pb facs="0202" n="132" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg132"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1140/250: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >House</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-15T23:00:00+00:00"
                            >November 15, 1918—11 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 15—7:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>110. For the President. I have just received the following communication from
                    Lord Derby: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Copy of telegram from Mr. Balfour to Lord Derby of November 15th. Very
                            urgent. Personal. Please convey following message from the King to
                            Colonel House for transmission to the President of the United States. ‘I
                            am delighted to hear that you contemplate shortly coming to England on
                            your way to France. It would give the Queen and myself the greatest
                            pleasure if you and Mrs. Wilson will be our guests at Buckingham Palace
                            during your stay in London.’”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
